## 1. ICON UTILITY CSS SOURCE

### File: [formats/components/src/utilities/icon/icon.css](formats/components/src/utilities/icon/icon.css#L1-L25)

**Lines 1-25**: The icon utility CSS establishes the mask-based painter mechanism:

```css
/**
 * @utility icon
 * @selector .pfx-icon
 * @summary The icon system: `.instui-icon` sizing plus the shared `-icon-<name>` painter that masks a glyph (in `currentColor`) before any element.
 * @modifier -icon-* — Set the glyph token (`--pantoken-glyph`) and render it via the shared painter (for example `-icon-search`).
 * @pseudo ::before — The glyph itself: a 1em box masked from `--pantoken-glyph` and filled with `currentColor`.
 * @accessibility The glyph is decorative, so mark it `aria-hidden="true"`; give it a `role` or label only when the icon conveys meaning on its own.
 * @example
 * <span class="instui-icon -icon-megaphone" aria-hidden="true"></span>
 */
@scope (.pfx-icon) {
  & {
    display: inline-flex;
  }
}

[class*="-icon-"]::before {
  content: "";
  display: inline-block;
  inline-size: 1em;
  block-size: 1em;
  flex: none;
  vertical-align: -0.125em;
  background: currentColor;
  -webkit-mask: var(--pantoken-glyph) center / contain no-repeat;
  mask: var(--pantoken-glyph) center / contain no-repeat;
}
```

**Key mechanism**:
- Generic selector `[class*="-icon-"]::before` catches any modifier with "-icon-" substring
- Creates a 1em square box (always 1:1 aspect ratio)
- Uses CSS `mask: var(--pantoken-glyph) center / contain no-repeat` to paint glyph
- Fills with `currentColor`, so icon color is inherited or controlled via `color` CSS property
- Vertical offset `-0.125em` aligns with text baseline

### File: [formats/components/src/utilities/icon-glyphs/index.ts](formats/components/src/utilities/icon-glyphs/index.ts#L1-L90)

**Lines 1-50**: Icon glyphs generation function:

```ts
export interface IconGlyphsOptions extends ComponentOptions {
  /**
   * Also emit the deprecated InstUI-prop glyph aliases (`-render-icon-<name>`, `-render-custom-icon-<name>`)
   * as functional aliases of `-icon-<name>`. Off by default — turning it on roughly doubles the sheet, so
   * enable it only when you need markup written against the old `renderIcon`/`renderCustomIcon` prop names
   * to keep rendering. The shipped `icons.css` is built with this on.
   */
  deprecatedAliases?: boolean;
  /**
   * Icon name → `--instui-icon-<name>` data-URI value. When given, the sheet also declares those
   * custom properties in `:root`, making it self-contained: the glyphs paint without a separate
   * token sheet loaded alongside. Omit to emit the lean mapping-only sheet.
   */
  values?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;
}

export function iconGlyphsCss(names: readonly string[], options: IconGlyphsOptions = {}): string {
  const prefix = options.prefix || "";
  const p = ns(prefix);
  void p; // glyph classes are prefix-independent modifiers (.-icon-<name>); consumed by any host.
  // The deprecated InstUI prop names that normalized to `-icon-<name>` (Pill's `renderIcon`, Alert's
  // `renderCustomIcon`). When `deprecatedAliases` is on, they're grouped onto the same rule as
  // FUNCTIONAL aliases (they set the same glyph var, and both contain the `-icon-` substring so the
  // shared painter + Alert's glyph pipe already fire) — otherwise omitted, which roughly halves the
  // sheet. They're `@deprecated` in each component's doc comment either way.
  const prefixes = options.deprecatedAliases
    ? ["-icon", "-render-icon", "-render-custom-icon"]
    : ["-icon"];
  const selectors = (name: string): string => prefixes.map((pre) => `.${pre}-${name}`).join(", ");
  const rules = names
    .map((name) => `${selectors(name)} { --pantoken-glyph: var(--instui-icon-${name}); }`)
    .join("\n");
  const header = `/* InstUI icon glyphs (@pantoken/components) — prefix: ${prefix} */\n`;
  if (!options.values) return `${header}${rules}\n`;
  const tokens = names
    .map((name) => {
      const value = options.values?.[name];
      if (value === undefined)
        throw new Error(`iconGlyphsCss: no value supplied for icon "${name}"`);
      return `  --instui-icon-${name}: ${value};`;
    })
    .join("\n");
  return `${header}:root {\n${tokens}\n}\n${rules}\n`;
}
```

**Key points**:
- Each icon is one CSS class: `.-icon-<name>` that sets `--pantoken-glyph` variable
- Optional `:root` token declarations make sheet self-contained (no separate token sheet needed)
- Generated output is a mapping layer only; painter is in shared `icon` utility
- Supports deprecated aliases for backwards compatibility with old component prop names

